+# Review
+
+- `src/shopcore/coupons.py:52` - Off-by-one: `>` lets `max_redemptions + 1` uses through; should be `>=`.
+- `src/shopcore/pricing.py:86` - Records every entered code, not the discounts applied in the quote, so unapplied codes are consumed.
+- `src/shopcore/coupons.py:25-27` - Guests are blocked from once-per-customer codes; they should be allowed to use them once.
+- `src/shopcore/coupons.py:35-36` - `max_redemptions=0` should be allowed so marketing can switch a coupon off; raising here is a regression.
+- `src/shopcore/coupons.py:43-45` - The counters are plain dicts and not thread-safe; concurrent checkouts can lose updates.
+- `src/shopcore/order.py:45` - `customer_id` should be required on every order, otherwise limits can be bypassed.
+- `src/shopcore/pricing.py:62-67` - The engine stores `redemptions` without checking that every limited code has a matching discount.
